# frozen_string_literal: true

=begin
  uc-director: the uber-combat hunt spine (D1).

  One loop, and nothing else:

    build itinerary -> choose leg -> write overlay -> run ONE bounded
    hunting-buddy stint -> measure it -> advance, repeat, or stop.

  Spec: notes/uber-combat/42-director-spec.md. Read section 0 first: seven
  corrections, three of which overturn an earlier decision. Runtime ground
  truth is in 41-director-runtime-facts.md and 41b-director-lifecycle-facts.md.

  ALL of the decision logic lives in lib/uc_director.rb and is pure and
  tested. This file is the WORLD ADAPTER and the presentation, nothing more --
  the same split uc-probe.lic keeps against lib/uc_probe.rb and uc-leg.lic
  keeps against LegOverlay/LegWriter. Every Script, DRC, DRStats, XMLData and
  File call the director makes lives in DirectorWorld below, so the core is
  driven by a plain double in spec/uc_director_spec.rb.

    ;uc-director            -- PLAN ONLY. Read-only. Issues no game command,
                               writes no file, launches nothing. Prints the
                               itinerary, leg 1's overlay YAML, the exact
                               launch line with its computed timeout, the
                               PREDICTED write decision, and the safety floor.
    ;uc-director run N      -- act. N is HOW MANY HUNTS to run, and it is
                               mandatory. It is NOT a leg number, even though
                               `;uc-leg go N` in this same suite takes one.
                               The director chooses the legs itself and
                               rotates the itinerary as skills grow.
    ;uc-director cycles N   -- act. N is how many FULL PASSES through the
                               itinerary to run. A pass is however many legs
                               the itinerary currently holds, so this is the
                               unit that stays meaningful when the leg count
                               changes underneath you.
    ;uc-director report     -- print the last run's stint table. In-memory
                               only in D1 (nothing is persisted; see below).

  Examples:
    ;uc-director
    ;uc-director run 8
    ;uc-director report

  THE DEFAULT MODE ACTS ON NOTHING ON PURPOSE. Every script in this project
  shipped read-only first and that discipline caught a real defect in each of
  the last three waves. The budget argument to `run` is REQUIRED and there is
  deliberately no unbounded mode: one stint is up to
  DURATION_MINUTES + STINT_SLACK_SECONDS of unattended combat, so `run` with
  no number would be an open-ended request to fight.

  WHY THE BUDGET COUNTS PRODUCTIVE STINTS, not attempts: a stint that never
  reached hunting-buddy's hunt loop taught the character nothing, so counting
  it would let `run 8` mean anything from zero to eight hunts. A stint that
  did not hunt increments that leg's failure counter instead (spec 6.3).

  NOTHING IS PERSISTED IN D1 (spec 7.3). No CharSettings, no Vars, no results
  file. The itinerary is re-derived from live skills on every start, so
  nothing a restart could leave stale is ever written. The single file this
  script touches is the character's `uc` profile overlay, written atomically
  by LegWriter and removed again in before_dying. `;uc-director report` reads
  a process-lifetime global, so it can report a run that finished in this
  Lich session and nothing older. Persistence is D4's job.

  THE STINT IS BOUNDED BY Script.run_child's timeout AND BY NOTHING ELSE.
  DRCT.find_empty_room's inner `pause 0.1 until room_id == Room.current.id`
  (common-travel.rb:323-324) has no timeout at all, and hunting-buddy walks
  into it from find_hunting_room? (hunting-buddy.lic:231) before the hunt
  starts. A blocked exit, a locked gate or a premium-gated zone wedges there
  forever with no message and no stop reason. run_child's `timeout:` is the
  only mechanism anywhere in that stack that breaks it, which is why this
  script never uses DRC.wait_for_script_to_complete (no timeout, and it
  returns instantly when start_script returns nil -- e.g. when hunting-buddy
  is ALREADY RUNNING -- which a director would read as a completed stint and
  then loop at full speed).
=end

# load (not require): edits to the uber-combat lib take effect without
# restarting Lich. Same rationale as uc-leg.lic's and uc-probe.lic's load
# blocks. Every UberCombat constant this file names MUST appear here --
# spec/uc_lic_loads_spec.rb is a standing guard against exactly the omission
# that once shipped `;uc-probe` with an unloaded LegSettings.
lib_dir = File.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'custom', 'lib')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_character.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_zone_table.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_zone_picker.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_leg_overlay.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_leg_settings.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_leg_writer.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_leg_tracker.rb')
load File.join(lib_dir, 'uc_director.rb')

require 'yaml'

# The world contract UberCombat::Director::Session is built against (spec
# section 3.1). One method per row of that table, no more: the fake in
# spec/uc_director_spec.rb and this class are checkable against one list, and
# a method that is not in the table does not belong here.
#
# This class also owns every DRC.message the LOOP produces, through #announce
# (spec 3.3). The core never reads anything back from it.
class DirectorWorld
  # SPEC SECTION 8. These three constants belong to the adapter because they
  # name Lich-facing values; every other director constant lives in the pure
  # core.
  #
  # HEALTH_FLOOR is 50, NOT uc-probe.lic's 75, and the difference is the whole
  # point. The probe's own comment (uc-probe.lic:113-117) says 75 is safe
  # BECAUSE THE PROBE NEVER FIGHTS -- any health loss at all means something
  # attacked it. This character fights for half an hour at a stretch, so a
  # post-stint health of 75 is a normal healthy outcome and reusing the
  # probe's value would abort the director after nearly every stint.
  # UNMEASURED, and it is open question (i): log health at every abort_reason
  # call across one run and read off the between-stint distribution.
  HEALTH_FLOOR = 50

  # Spirit does not fall from ordinary combat, so the probe's value transfers
  # unchanged (uc-probe.lic:119).
  SPIRIT_FLOOR = 50

  # Verbatim from uc-probe.lic:408. gosafe.lic is 14 lines and has no timeout
  # of its own (it ends in DRCT.walk_to settings.safe_room), so an unbounded
  # recovery could outlive the run it was recovering from.
  GOSAFE_TIMEOUT = 300

  # How long to wait for a killed go2 to actually be gone. A runtime kill is
  # ASYNCHRONOUS (script.rb:1781-1783), so a caller that does not wait can
  # start the next stint while the old walker is still tearing down.
  WALKER_STOP_TIMEOUT = 10

  # The return shape of #run_stint (spec 3.2). The Struct itself is DEFINED in
  # lib/uc_director.rb, not here, and this adapter only builds instances of it.
  # Spec 3.2 says "built by the adapter", which is true of the values and was
  # briefly read as true of the declaration too -- so both files defined an
  # identical Struct. Two declarations of one contract drift, and the drift is
  # silent: the core reads the fields duck-typed, so a field added on one side
  # only would read as nil on the other rather than raise. One owner, in lib/,
  # where spec/uc_lic_loads_spec.rb's constant guard can see it.
  Launch = UberCombat::Director::Launch

  attr_reader :abort_detail, :last_itinerary, :last_stop, :refusals

  def initialize
    # get_settings with NO flex suffix, deliberately -- and here the reason is
    # sharper than it is in uc-leg.lic:73-79. This script WRITES the character's
    # `uc` flex file. get_settings(['uc']) would merge that generated overlay
    # back in, so the picker and the overlay engine would be configured partly
    # out of the previous leg's own output. uc_weapons and uc_spells live in
    # <Character>-setup.yaml and never in a flex file, so the plain call is
    # also the correct one on its own terms.
    settings = get_settings

    @character = UberCombat::Character.new
    @zone_table = UberCombat::ZoneTable.from_game_data

    # Constructed exactly as uc-leg.lic:87-97 does it, and for the same
    # reasons documented there: the picker needs the account tier (a profile
    # value, so there is nothing to build it with until settings are in hand)
    # and leaving the argument off silently gates a premium character out of
    # the zones they paid for.
    refuse_without_weapons(settings)
    refuse_unknown_skills(settings)
    refuse_bad_creature_flags(settings)
    warn_about_max_skills(settings)
    warn_about_duration(settings)
    @picker = UberCombat::ZonePicker.new(
      @character, @zone_table,
      UberCombat::LegSettings.premium(settings),
      province: UberCombat::LegSettings.in_province_only(settings),
      max_skills_per_leg: UberCombat::LegSettings.max_skills_per_leg(settings),
      trainable_skills: UberCombat::LegSettings.trainable_skills(settings),
      creature_flags: UberCombat::LegSettings.require_creature_flags(settings)
    )
    @overlay_engine = UberCombat::LegOverlay.new(
      @character,
      UberCombat::LegSettings.weapons(settings),
      uc_spells: UberCombat::LegSettings.spells(settings),
      known_spell_names: UberCombat::LegSettings.known_spell_names(get_data('spells'))
    )

    @abort_detail = nil
    # Presentation memory only. The core never reads these back; they exist so
    # that the :stopped report can name WHY a run ended without the core
    # having to carry the itinerary and the refusal map through its own return
    # shape (spec 6.5 requires both to be printed).
    @last_itinerary = nil
    @last_stop = nil
    @refusals = {}
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- clock

  # Only ever used for elapsed arithmetic, never memoised.
  def now
    Time.now
  end

  # ------------------------------------------------------------ lifecycle

  # THE ONLY PAUSE-HONOURING CALL IN THE WHOLE LOOP (correction C3).
  #
  # 41b Q1 claimed a paused script blocks at "most global defs (echo, fput,
  # pause, waitfor, ...)". Two of those are wrong and they are the two a
  # director would otherwise be built out of: `pause` (global_defs.rb:1399-1409)
  # is a bare sleep with suffix parsing and never calls Script.current, and
  # DRC.message reaches _respond (global_defs.rb:1825) which does not either.
  # The enforcement point is
  # `sleep 0.2 while script.paused? and not script.ignore_pause` INSIDE
  # Script.current (script.rb:1026). A loop made of pause, DRC.message,
  # Script.run_child and pure Ruby therefore honours `;p uc-director` NOWHERE.
  #
  # So the checkpoint is explicit, and it is one bare Script.current at the top
  # of every cycle. Note what it does NOT do: a pause issued mid-stint does not
  # suspend run_child's join (Script#join waits on a ConditionVariable and never
  # routes through Script.current, script.rb:1892-1921), so the stint still ends
  # on its own deadline and the pause takes effect here, one cycle later.
  def checkpoint
    Script.current
    nil
  end

  # The safety floor, run at the top of every cycle BEFORE the leg is chosen
  # (spec 7.1). Shape copied verbatim from uc-probe.lic:372-380; the values
  # are not (see HEALTH_FLOOR above).
  #
  # Every read here is a cached class-variable or XML read with no game
  # command, which is what makes it cheap enough to run every cycle.
  # DRCH.check_health is deliberately excluded for the reason
  # uc-probe.lic:365-368 gives: it issues a live `health` command.
  #
  # checkbleeding is in the probe's ladder and is deliberately NOT in this
  # one. Bleeding after a hunt is routine, it is tended in stride, and
  # hunting-buddy already ends its own hunt on it
  # (hunting-buddy.lic:590-594, stop_hunting_if_bleeding: true in base.yaml).
  # A hard director abort on bleeding would end most runs one stint in.
  #
  # :budget_spent is not here either: the budget is loop state, not a world
  # condition, and the core's own `while productive < budget` owns it.
  def abort_reason
    return note(:dead) if dead?
    return note(:health, DRStats.health) if DRStats.health < HEALTH_FLOOR
    return note(:spirit, DRStats.spirit) if DRStats.spirit < SPIRIT_FLOOR

    nil
  end

  # --------------------------------------------------------------- picker

  def build_itinerary
    @last_itinerary = @picker.build_itinerary
  end

  # ------------------------------------------------------------- overlay

  # May raise ArgumentError on an unknown stance policy
  # (uc_leg_overlay.rb:283) or a priority defence outside VALID_PRIORITY_DEFENSES
  # (:300-302). Both are invariant guards that should never fire, and the core
  # rescues them into a :overlay_error stop rather than letting them kill the
  # script after a leg was already selected (spec 6.1, 6.2).
  def overlay_for(leg, duration:)
    @overlay_engine.build(leg, duration: duration)
  end

  # THE ONE ABSOLUTE PATH this script ever targets, derived verbatim from
  # uc-leg.lic:327 through SetupFiles' own private resolution rather than
  # hardcoded, so it cannot drift from what get_settings(['uc']) inside
  # hunting-buddy will actually read. $setupfiles is the process-wide instance
  # every get_settings / get_data call already goes through
  # (global_defs.rb:68).
  #
  # Memoised because it cannot change while the script runs and because
  # uc-leg.lic:311-326 insists there be exactly one place a target path is
  # computed. There is deliberately no CLI argument anywhere in this file that
  # can override or extend it: the only value `run` accepts from a person is a
  # stint COUNT.
  def overlay_path
    @overlay_path ||= File.join($setupfiles.send(:scripts_profiles_path),
                                $setupfiles.send(:to_character_filename, 'uc'))
  end

  # LegWriter.read_first_line is private_class_method (uc_leg_writer.rb:134),
  # so the adapter performs this read itself and hands the result to the
  # public, pure LegWriter.decide. Needed only by plan mode, which uses it to
  # PREDICT a :gaps or :foreign_file refusal without writing a byte.
  #
  # An existing-but-empty file reads back "", which is neither nil nor MARKER
  # and therefore correctly predicts :foreign_file (uc_leg_writer.rb:87-89).
  def existing_first_line
    return nil unless File.exist?(overlay_path)

    File.open(overlay_path, 'r') { |handle| handle.gets }
  end

  # Returns a LegWriter::Result. A refusal is a first-class return, never an
  # exception (uc_leg_writer.rb:65-72). A REAL I/O failure inside the atomic
  # write does raise (:165-172) and this method lets it propagate: the core
  # rescues it into a :write_error stop.
  def write_overlay(overlay)
    UberCombat::LegWriter.write(overlay, overlay_path)
  end

  # Called only from before_dying. Never deletes a foreign file: the marker
  # check is the same byte-for-byte comparison LegWriter itself makes before
  # overwriting (uc_leg_writer.rb:112, MARKER at :40). Idempotent, one
  # filesystem call, and it swallows its own errors because a teardown path
  # must never raise.
  def remove_overlay
    return false unless File.exist?(overlay_path)
    return false unless existing_first_line == UberCombat::LegWriter::MARKER

    File.delete(overlay_path)
    true
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  # -------------------------------------------------------------- tracker

  # One tracker per leg. The core replaces it whenever the leg changes or the
  # itinerary is rebuilt -- README rule 6: LegTracker owns no cadence, so it
  # must never be handed one.
  #
  # leg[:zone_key] is a String (uc_zone_table.rb:158-159), which is what
  # ZoneTable#zone is keyed on.
  def tracker_for(leg)
    UberCombat::LegTracker.new(
      @character,
      zone: @zone_table.zone(leg[:zone_key]),
      skills: leg[:skills]
    )
  end

  # Both reads are cached XML with no command cost (uc_character.rb:90-92,
  # :104-106), which is why the core can afford to re-snapshot immediately
  # after the pause checkpoint rather than trusting a value read before a
  # pause that may have lasted an hour (spec 7.2, requirement 2).
  def snapshot(skills)
    skills.to_h do |skill|
      [skill, { rank: @character.rank_of(skill), mindstate: @character.mindstate_of(skill) }]
    end
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- stint

  # ONE bounded hunting-buddy stint. See the header for why run_child and not
  # DRC.wait_for_script_to_complete.
  #
  # $HUNTING_BUDDY IS CLEARED FIRST, AND THAT IS NOT HYGIENE -- IT IS THE
  # WHOLE BASIS OF THE MEASUREMENT. The global is assigned at
  # hunting-buddy.lic:729, AFTER HuntingBuddy.new returns. If the constructor
  # raises -- and it does, with "no implicit conversion of nil into Array"
  # from @hunting_info += infos (:122) whenever the merged profile has no
  # hunting_info -- the assignment never happens and the global still holds
  # the object from the PREVIOUS run in this Lich process, complete with that
  # run's hunt_stop_reason. Nothing else clears it: hunting-buddy's
  # before_dying does not, and Lich's teardown clears only per-Script state.
  #
  # THE OBJECT IS TESTED, NOT THE REASON. NilClass#method_missing is patched to
  # return nil (nilclass.rb:9-11), so $HUNTING_BUDDY.hunt_stop_reason on a nil
  # global returns nil SILENTLY -- indistinguishable from a real nil reason and
  # from a typo'd accessor name. `&.` buys nothing here. Only holder.nil?
  # separates them.
  #
  # A non-nil reason is proof the hunt loop actually ran, because
  # @hunt_stop_reason is assigned only inside `hunt`, at hunting-buddy.lic:576
  # and below. That is a claim about control flow, not about why the hunt
  # stopped, and it is the only use the classifier makes of it.
  def run_stint(timeout)
    $HUNTING_BUDDY = nil
    # 'uc' IS A STRING, NOT ['uc']. This cost a whole run to find, and it
    # fails silently, so it is worth spelling out.
    #
    # Script.start's argument dispatch (script.rb:86-105) accepts args[1] as
    # a String (script arguments) or a Hash (options) and falls through to a
    # bare `next nil` for anything else -- the entire error handling is a
    # `# fixme: error` comment, so an Array produces NO message anywhere.
    # start_child then returns nil and run_child converts that into a
    # StartError, which looks exactly like "hunting-buddy is already
    # running".
    #
    # The array form is not wrong everywhere, which is what makes it a trap.
    # start_script(name, ['uc']) IS correct, because that global def joins
    # the array itself before calling Script.start (global_defs.rb:19-24).
    # Script.start does no such conversion. Do not "restore" the brackets.
    child = Script.run_child('hunting-buddy', 'uc', timeout: timeout)
    launch(:completed,
           completed_successfully: child.completed_successfully?,
           exit_error: child.exit_error)
  rescue Script::StartError
    # start_child returned nil: the file is missing, Lich is shutting down,
    # construction failed, or -- the important one -- hunting-buddy is ALREADY
    # RUNNING (script.rb:136, __begin_start returning :duplicate at :747).
    # None of those is fixed by retrying, so the core stops the run.
    launch(:start_error)
  rescue Script::TimeoutError
    # join returned nil, then kill_sync ran, THEN the raise. The doc comment
    # guarantees that ordering (script.rb:987-989), so no unsupervised CHILD
    # survives this. hunting-buddy's own before_dying still stopped
    # combat-trainer on the way out (:707-718, run inside __run_kill_cleanup).
    #
    # A WALKER is not a child, which is why stop_walkers exists. See its
    # comment: the kill cascade cannot reach go2, and an orphaned go2 turns
    # the NEXT stint into the very hang this timeout exists to break.
    stop_walkers
    #
    # What a timeout does NOT do is walk the character home: the
    # DRCT.walk_to(safe_room) at hunting-buddy.lic:273 is in main, after the
    # loop, and a killed script never reaches it. D1 leaves the character
    # standing in the zone -- the next cycle's abort_reason runs before
    # anything else and the next stint does its own travel. Open question (j).
    launch(:timeout)
  rescue StandardError => e
    launch(:error, exit_error: e)
  end

  # --------------------------------------------------------------- walkers

  # Stop a walker the stint teardown could not reach. Returns true when
  # nothing is walking any more.
  #
  # THE KILL CASCADE DOES NOT REACH go2. walk_to starts it with
  # start_script (common-travel.rb:223), which is Script.start
  # (global_defs.rb:19-24) and NOT start_child, so go2 is a sibling of
  # hunting-buddy rather than a child, and Script#kill's __stop_children
  # (script.rb:2052) never sees it. hunting-buddy's own before_dying stops
  # only combat-trainer (hunting-buddy.lic tail).
  #
  # Left running, go2 keeps walking toward the room hunting-buddy wanted
  # while the director believes the stint is over. The next stint's walk_to
  # then calls start_script('go2') a second time, Lich refuses the duplicate
  # and returns nil (script.rb:740-747), walk_to's `while
  # Script.running.include?(script_handle)` is false immediately because the
  # handle is nil, and find_empty_room is handed a character who never
  # arrives -- the unbounded `pause 0.1 until room_id == Room.current.id` at
  # common-travel.rb:324. That is the exact hang the timeout exists to break,
  # re-entered through the back door one stint later.
  #
  # bescort is deliberately NOT killed. A crossing is bounded and ends by
  # itself, killing one mid-ferry can strand the character on the far side,
  # and walk_to already holds its own 90-second stall timer off for as long
  # as bescort runs (common-travel.rb:253) -- so a later stint tolerates one
  # that is still finishing. Only the walker that would keep CHOOSING rooms
  # is stopped.
  def stop_walkers
    return true unless Script.running?('go2')

    DRC.message('uc-director: stopping an orphaned go2 left over from the stint.')
    kill_script('go2')
    waited = 0
    while Script.running?('go2') && waited < WALKER_STOP_TIMEOUT
      pause 0.5
      waited += 0.5
    end

    return true unless Script.running?('go2')

    DRC.message(format('uc-director: go2 is STILL running %d s after the kill. ' \
                       'The next stint may not travel correctly.', WALKER_STOP_TIMEOUT))
    false
  end

  # -------------------------------------------------------------- recovery

  # Only ever called by the core, and only for a SAFETY stop
  # (Director.safety_stop?). A spent budget is the ordinary end of a bounded
  # run and must not walk the character across the continent.
  #
  # Wrapped in rescue StandardError for uc-probe.lic:693-696's reason, which
  # applies here word for word: never let the recovery path be the thing that
  # kills the run's report.
  #
  # NEVER fput('exit'). hunting-buddy.lic:585-589 sends the game command
  # `exit` on low health, logging the character out, with no break after it.
  # The director's ladder is: stop the child, gosafe under a timeout, report,
  # stop -- leaving the character parked and still logged in.
  def recover(reason)
    DRC.message(format('-- Safety stop (%s): running gosafe --', reason))
    # Before gosafe, not after. gosafe is 14 lines ending in DRCT.walk_to
    # (dr-scripts/gosafe.lic:11), so it starts a go2 of its own -- and an
    # orphaned walker still running would make Lich refuse that one as a
    # duplicate (script.rb:740-747), leaving the character walking toward the
    # hunting zone during what is supposed to be the retreat from it.
    stop_walkers
    Script.run_child('gosafe', timeout: GOSAFE_TIMEOUT)
    DRC.message('  gosafe finished.', false)
    nil
  rescue StandardError => e
    DRC.message(format('  gosafe did not complete (%s: %s). Recover by hand.', e.class, e.message))
    nil
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------- presentation

  # ONE method rather than a family, so the fake in the spec is a single
  # recorder (spec 3.3). The core never reads anything back from it.
  #
  # The signature accepts the payload either as keywords -- which is how the
  # core's `announce(:verdict, leg_index: i, ...)` call sites read -- or as an
  # explicit Hash, so neither calling convention can break the adapter.
  def announce(event, payload = {}, **extra)
    data = payload.merge(extra)
    case event
    when :plan then render_plan(data)
    when :leg_selected then render_leg_selected(data)
    when :leg_refused then render_leg_refused(data)
    when :leg_skipped then render_leg_skipped(data)
    when :stint_ended then render_stint_ended(data)
    when :verdict then render_verdict(data)
    when :stopped then render_stopped(data)
    else
      DRC.message(format('uc-director: unhandled event %s %s', event, data.inspect))
    end
    nil
  end

  # One stint as a single line. A class method because ;uc-director report
  # renders the same rows from the recorded run, and the two must never
  # disagree about what a stint looked like.
  def self.stint_line(stint)
    format('  leg %-3d %-24s %-16s %6.0fs stop=%-14s outcome=%s',
           stint.leg_index.to_i + 1,
           stint.leg.is_a?(Hash) ? stint.leg[:zone_key] : '?',
           stint.classification,
           stint.elapsed.to_f,
           stint.stop_reason || 'none',
           stint.outcome)
  end

  # The rank and mindstate movement the classifier actually measured. This is
  # the data open questions (e) and (f) are answered from -- MIN_PRODUCTIVE_STINT
  # and BARREN_LIMIT are both unmeasured guesses today -- so it is printed on
  # every stint rather than only on a surprising one.
  def self.stint_deltas(stint)
    skills = stint.leg.is_a?(Hash) ? Array(stint.leg[:skills]) : []
    skills.map do |skill|
      before = stint.before.is_a?(Hash) ? stint.before[skill] : nil
      after = stint.after.is_a?(Hash) ? stint.after[skill] : nil
      next format('    %-18s (not measured)', skill) if before.nil? || after.nil?

      format('    %-18s rank %8.1f to %8.1f   mind %2d to %2d',
             skill, before[:rank].to_f, after[:rank].to_f,
             before[:mindstate].to_i, after[:mindstate].to_i)
    end
  end

  private

  # A skill name that is not a real skill is a TYPO, not a decision. The valid
  # names are a closed set, so this is checkable, and leaving it uncheckable
  # would mean `Small Edge` reads as "I do not train Small Edged" -- the one
  # thing the person who typed it did not mean.
  def refuse_unknown_skills(settings)
    unknown = UberCombat::LegSettings.unknown_skill_names(settings)
    return if unknown.empty?

    DRC.message('uc: uc_settings names skills that do not exist. Fix these and run again:')
    unknown.each do |row|
      guess = UberCombat::LegSettings.closest_skill_name(row[:name])
      DRC.message(format('    %s: %s%s', row[:source], row[:name],
                         guess ? format('   did you mean %s', guess) : ''), false)
    end
    exit
  end

  # require_creature_flags is the guild's rule about what it may hunt, so a
  # mistake in it is fatal. A mistyped gate that was quietly dropped would send
  # an empath at living creatures or a necromancer at undead, and nothing would
  # say why.
  def refuse_bad_creature_flags(settings)
    errors = UberCombat::LegSettings.creature_flag_errors(settings)
    return if errors.empty?

    DRC.message('uc: uc_settings require_creature_flags is wrong. Fix it and run again:')
    errors.each { |line| DRC.message("    #{line}", false) }
    exit
  end

  # An empty weapons catalogue is the one catalogue error that stays fatal.
  # Omitting a weapon means "I do not train that one"; omitting all of them
  # leaves nothing to hunt with, and every leg would be built for a skill with
  # no weapon to swing. Raising here beats an itinerary of refusals.
  def refuse_without_weapons(settings)
    return unless UberCombat::LegSettings.no_weapons?(settings)

    DRC.message('uc: uc_settings has no `weapons` entries, so there is nothing to train with.')
    DRC.message('  Add at least one skill-to-weapon pair under uc_settings weapons.', false)
    DRC.message('  Leaving a weapon OUT is fine and means you do not train it.', false)
    # exit, not raise: this is a configuration mistake, and a Lich error trace
    # would bury the three lines above it that say what to do.
    exit
  end

  # A present-but-unusable max_skills_per_leg falls back to the default, which
  # is the safe direction but is also invisible. Say so once, or a person who
  # wrote `max_skills_per_leg: "3"` sees the default itinerary and concludes
  # the setting does nothing.
  def warn_about_max_skills(settings)
    return unless UberCombat::LegSettings.bad_max_skills_per_leg?(settings)

    DRC.message('uc: max_skills_per_leg must be a positive whole number. ' \
                'Ignoring it and using the default.')
  end

  # Zero is the one that would really hurt if taken literally: hunting-buddy
  # checks `(counter / 60) >= duration` (hunting-buddy.lic:622), which is true
  # on the first pass, so every stint would end at once having taught nothing
  # and every leg would be skipped after two failures.
  def warn_about_duration(settings)
    return unless UberCombat::LegSettings.bad_hunt_duration_minutes?(settings)

    DRC.message('uc-director: hunt_duration_minutes must be a positive whole number. ' \
                'Ignoring it and using the default.')
  end

  def note(reason, value = nil)
    @abort_detail = value
    reason
  end

  def launch(outcome, completed_successfully: false, exit_error: nil)
    holder = $HUNTING_BUDDY
    Launch.new(outcome: outcome,
               stop_reason: holder.nil? ? nil : holder.hunt_stop_reason,
               completed_successfully: completed_successfully,
               exit_error: exit_error)
  end

  # ------------------------------------------------------- event renderers

  # Plan mode's whole output except the safety floor, which UcDirector prints
  # itself because it owns the floor's presentation on the refusal path too.
  def render_plan(data)
    render_itinerary(data[:itinerary])
    leg = data[:leg]
    return if leg.nil?

    DRC.message(format('-- Leg %d is the leg `run` would take first --', data[:leg_index].to_i + 1))
    DRC.message(format('  skills:       %s', Array(leg[:skills]).join(', ')), false)
    DRC.message(format('  zone_key:     %s', leg[:zone_key]), false)
    DRC.message(format('  stance:       policy=%s key=%s',
                       leg[:stance][:policy], leg[:stance][:key]), false)
    render_plan_overlay(data)
    render_plan_launch(data)
  end

  def render_plan_overlay(data)
    overlay = data[:overlay]
    DRC.message('-- Overlay this leg would write --')
    if overlay.nil?
      DRC.message('  (overlay could not be built; see the error above)', false)
      return
    end

    print_yaml(overlay.settings)
    render_gaps(overlay.gaps)
    DRC.message('-- Overlay file target --')
    DRC.message("  #{data[:path]}", false)
    render_predicted_decision(data[:decision])
  end

  # The PREDICTED write outcome, from the pure, public LegWriter.decide fed
  # this file's real first line -- so plan mode reports :gaps or :foreign_file
  # before a single byte is written anywhere.
  def render_predicted_decision(decision)
    if decision.nil?
      DRC.message('  PREDICTED WRITE: unknown (no overlay to decide on)', false)
      return
    end

    if decision.write
      DRC.message('  PREDICTED WRITE: WOULD WRITE', false)
      return
    end

    DRC.message(format('  PREDICTED WRITE: WOULD REFUSE (%s)', decision.reason), false)
    return unless decision.reason == :foreign_file

    DRC.message('  A file already exists at this path and carries no uc-leg marker line.', false)
    DRC.message('  Every leg targets that one path, so this refusal stops the WHOLE run.', false)
    DRC.message('  Remove or rename it by hand first.', false)
  end

  def render_plan_launch(data)
    DRC.message('-- The stint `run` would launch --')
    DRC.message(format("  Script.run_child('hunting-buddy', 'uc', timeout: %d)", data[:timeout].to_i), false)
    DRC.message(format('  duration: %d minutes, written into the overlay as the :duration: key', data[:duration].to_i), false)
    # NOT "duration plus slack", which was the old wording and which framed
    # this as a second opinion on the hunt. hunting-buddy already bounds its
    # own hunting (hunting-buddy.lic:622). This bounds the parts NOTHING
    # times: the tannery trip, the restock, travel, and the walk home.
    DRC.message(format('  timeout:  %d seconds -- the outer bound on the whole stint, including ' \
                       'the untimed travel and restock around the hunt', data[:timeout].to_i), false)
    DRC.message('  Nothing below this line has run. This mode issues no game command.', false)
  end

  # Verbatim presentation from uc-leg.lic:233-249, which is itself verbatim
  # from uc-zones.lic, so all three diagnostics report the same itinerary the
  # same way and can never appear to disagree about what the picker returned.
  def render_itinerary(itinerary)
    DRC.message('-- Itinerary (build_itinerary) --')
    if itinerary.nil? || itinerary.legs.empty?
      DRC.message('  (no legs)', false)
      render_unplaced(itinerary&.unplaced)
      return
    end

    itinerary.legs.each_with_index do |leg, index|
      DRC.message(format('  Leg %d: %s', index + 1, leg[:skills].join(', ')), false)
      DRC.message(format('    zone=%-24s stance=%-12s', leg[:zone_key], leg[:stance][:policy]), false)
    end
    render_unplaced(itinerary.unplaced)
    render_unresolved_premium(itinerary.unresolved_premium)
  end

  # README rule 3: a skill that gets no zone is reported with a reason. A
  # silent cap reads as full coverage. The reason is a closed set
  # (uc_zone_picker.rb:240-254) and each value names a different fix.
  def render_unplaced(records)
    return if records.nil? || records.empty?

    DRC.message('  -- Skills with no leg --', false)
    records.each do |record|
      DRC.message(format('    %-18s reason=%-22s %s', record[:skill], record[:reason], record[:detail]), false)
    end
  end

  # The premium gate falls OPEN on a zone nobody has annotated yet
  # (uc_zone_picker.rb:84-86). That is only defensible while every unknown an
  # actual leg leans on gets named, which is what this prints.
  def render_unresolved_premium(records)
    return if records.nil? || records.empty?

    DRC.message('  -- Premium status unknown for these leg zones --', false)
    records.each do |record|
      DRC.message(format('    %-24s skills=%s', record[:zone_key], record[:detail][:skills].join(', ')), false)
    end
    DRC.message('    If a stint cannot travel to one of these, it is premium only.', false)
  end

  def render_leg_selected(data)
    DRC.message(format('***STATUS*** uc-director: leg %d of %d -- %s',
                       data[:leg_index].to_i + 1, data[:count].to_i,
                       Array(data[:leg][:skills]).join(', ')))
    DRC.message(format('  zone=%s  duration=%d min  timeout=%d s',
                       data[:leg][:zone_key], data[:duration].to_i, data[:timeout].to_i), false)
  end

  # A :gaps refusal takes this leg out for the rest of the run: retrying
  # without a profile edit refuses identically. The gap records are what a
  # person actually acts on, so they are printed rather than counted.
  def render_leg_refused(data)
    index = data[:leg_index].to_i
    @refusals[index] = data[:reason]
    DRC.message(format('***STATUS*** uc-director: leg %d refused (%s) -- skipping it for this run',
                       index + 1, data[:reason]))
    render_gaps(data[:gaps] || [])
  end

  # A skipped leg is a real, actionable finding, so it names the leg, its zone
  # and whether that zone was riding an unchecked premium flag (spec 6.3).
  def render_leg_skipped(data)
    index = data[:leg_index].to_i
    @refusals[index] = :failed_to_hunt
    leg = data[:leg]
    DRC.message(format('***STATUS*** uc-director: leg %d skipped after %d consecutive failed stint(s)',
                       index + 1, data[:failures].to_i))
    DRC.message(format('  skills=%s  zone=%s', Array(leg[:skills]).join(', '), leg[:zone_key]), false)
    return unless unresolved_premium?(leg[:zone_key])

    DRC.message('  That zone has an UNCHECKED premium flag, which is a likely cause:', false)
    DRC.message('  a non-premium character cannot travel there at all.', false)
  end

  def render_stint_ended(data)
    stint = data[:stint]
    DRC.message(format('***STATUS*** uc-director: stint ended -- %s', stint.classification))
    DRC.message(DirectorWorld.stint_line(stint), false)
    DirectorWorld.stint_deltas(stint).each { |line| DRC.message(line, false) }
    return unless stint.stop_reason.nil?

    # nil means "we cannot tell whether it hunted", never "advance the leg".
    # Eleven paths in hunting-buddy exit with no reason set (correction C7),
    # including a Kernel exit at :386 that Lich records as a SUCCESSFUL exit --
    # byte-for-byte indistinguishable from a clean stint by the Script handle
    # alone. Only the measurement above separates them.
    DRC.message('  No stop reason was set, so the hunt loop may never have run.', false)
    DRC.message('  Classification above came from elapsed time and skill movement only.', false)
  end

  # The decision is a Director::Decision(action:, reason:), not a bare Symbol.
  # Printing the struct itself would put "#<struct ...>" through DRC.message,
  # which strips anything shaped like a tag -- so the one line saying why a leg
  # ended would come out mangled. The reason is the point of the line: four
  # separate rules reach :advance and they mean different things to a reader.
  # :rank_max_exceeded is success, :mindlocked is success, :no_gain_limit is a
  # zone that stopped paying, and :stint_cap is a deliberate hand-off so the
  # other legs get their turn.
  def render_verdict(data)
    verdict = data[:verdict]
    reason = verdict.respond_to?(:reason) ? verdict.reason : nil
    status = verdict.respond_to?(:status) ? verdict.status : verdict
    decision = data[:decision]
    action = decision.respond_to?(:action) ? decision.action : decision
    why = decision.respond_to?(:reason) ? decision.reason : nil
    DRC.message(format('  tracker=%s%s  decision=%s%s',
                       status, reason ? format(' (%s)', reason) : '',
                       action, why ? format(' (%s)', why) : ''), false)
  end

  # The one report every run ends with. It names the reason, and for the
  # reasons that need a human to do something it says what.
  def render_stopped(data)
    stints = Array(data[:stints])
    @last_stop = { reason: data[:reason], detail: data[:detail] || @abort_detail, stints: stints }
    DRC.message(format('***STATUS*** uc-director: STOPPED -- %s%s', data[:reason],
                       @last_stop[:detail] ? format(' (%s)', @last_stop[:detail]) : ''))
    render_tally(stints)
    render_stop_advice(data[:reason])
  end

  def render_tally(stints)
    DRC.message(format('  stints run: %d', stints.size), false)
    productive = stints.count { |stint| stint.classification == :productive }
    DRC.message(format('  productive: %d', productive), false)
    stints.group_by(&:classification).sort_by { |name, _| name.to_s }.each do |name, list|
      DRC.message(format('    %-16s %3d', name, list.size), false)
    end
  end

  def render_stop_advice(reason)
    case reason
    when :no_legs
      DRC.message('  The picker returned no legs at all. The reasons are listed above:', false)
      DRC.message('  each unplaced skill names the FIRST stage that emptied its zone set.', false)
      render_unplaced(@last_itinerary&.unplaced)
    when :all_legs_refused
      render_refusal_table
    when :launch_refused
      DRC.message('  Script.run_child could not start hunting-buddy. Check, in this order:', false)
      DRC.message('    1. hunting-buddy is ALREADY RUNNING (something else is driving this character)', false)
      DRC.message('    2. hunting-buddy.lic is missing from the scripts directory', false)
      DRC.message('    3. Lich is shutting down', false)
      DRC.message('    4. the launch arguments are the wrong CLASS. Script.start takes script', false)
      DRC.message("       arguments as a String ('uc'), and silently refuses an Array (['uc'])", false)
      DRC.message('       with no message at all -- script.rb:86-105 falls through to a bare nil.', false)
      DRC.message('       This one looked exactly like cause 1 for a whole run.', false)
      DRC.message('  None of those is fixed by retrying, which is why the run stopped instead.', false)
    when :foreign_file
      DRC.message("  A file at #{overlay_path} was not generated by this suite.", false)
      DRC.message('  Every leg targets that one path, so no leg can run until it is moved.', false)
    when :write_error
      DRC.message("  Writing #{overlay_path} raised. Check the directory is writable and has space.", false)
    when :overlay_error
      DRC.message('  The overlay engine raised ArgumentError. That is an invariant guard', false)
      DRC.message('  (an unknown stance policy or priority defence) and it is a bug, not a setting.', false)
    end
  end

  def render_refusal_table
    DRC.message('  Every leg in the itinerary was refused. Per leg:', false)
    legs = @last_itinerary ? @last_itinerary.legs : []
    legs.each_with_index do |leg, index|
      DRC.message(format('    Leg %-3d %-24s %s', index + 1, leg[:zone_key],
                         @refusals[index] || 'refused'), false)
    end
  end

  def render_gaps(gaps)
    if gaps.nil? || gaps.empty?
      DRC.message('  -- Gaps: none --', false)
      return
    end

    DRC.message('  -- Gaps: this leg cannot be written --', false)
    gaps.each do |gap|
      DRC.message(format('    %-16s reason=%-20s %s', gap[:skill], gap[:reason], gap[:detail]), false)
    end
  end

  def unresolved_premium?(zone_key)
    records = @last_itinerary&.unresolved_premium
    return false if records.nil?

    records.any? { |record| record[:zone_key] == zone_key }
  end

  # DRC.message takes one line at a time -- it has no multi-line contract of
  # its own, unlike Lich::Messaging.mono -- so the dump is split here rather
  # than handed over with embedded newlines. The '...' terminator is
  # uc-leg.lic:290-296's and it earns its place: without it the next line sits
  # at the same indent and reads as one more YAML key.
  def print_yaml(settings)
    settings.to_yaml.each_line { |line| DRC.message(line.chomp, false) }
    DRC.message('...', false)
  end
end

# Owns the three modes, the banner, the preflight refusals and the run
# record. No decision logic -- every verdict, every classification and the
# whole loop belong to UberCombat::Director (lib/uc_director.rb).
class UcDirector
  # ;uc-director report has to survive the script that produced the run
  # exiting, and D1 persists NOTHING (spec 7.3), so the record lives in a
  # process-lifetime global. It outlives the script and dies with Lich, which
  # is exactly the "in-memory only in D1" the spec asks for. It is
  # deliberately NOT CharSettings: persistence across a restart is D4's job
  # and writing a half-designed shape now is what D4 would have to undo.
  #
  # $UC_DIRECTOR is the ;e control handle, mirroring t2.lic:249-251. This is a
  # SECOND global because before_dying clears that handle, and a report that
  # vanished the moment the run finished would be no report at all.

  # Reachable through $UC_DIRECTOR for ;e inspection while a run is going.
  attr_reader :world

  def initialize
    @world = nil
  end

  # PLAN ONLY. Issues no game command, walks nowhere, launches nothing, and
  # writes no file. The one filesystem call is a READ of the overlay path's
  # first line, so that a :foreign_file refusal is predicted here instead of
  # discovered halfway through a run.
  def plan
    banner
    world = DirectorWorld.new
    itinerary = world.build_itinerary
    leg = itinerary.legs.first
    world.announce(:plan, plan_payload(world, itinerary, leg))
    report_floor(world)
  end

  def run(budget, unit: :stints)
    banner
    world = DirectorWorld.new
    @world = world
    return unless preflight(world)

    # Registered only in this mode. before_dying in plan mode would give a
    # read-only script a teardown that deletes a file.
    #
    # WHAT IS IN HERE IS THE WHOLE LIST (spec 7.1): remove the overlay we
    # wrote, drop the control handle. No walk_to, no gosafe, no bput, no
    # start_script, no unbounded loop. gosafe CANNOT live here -- once
    # @@shutdown_started is set, __begin_start returns :shutdown and the
    # launcher answers "cannot start X while shutting down" (script.rb:743,
    # :132-135) -- and it must not on time grounds either: a shutdown kill
    # runs at_exit procs INLINE under a ~20 second drain and a 60 second
    # Process.exit!(1) watchdog.
    #
    # Stopping the hunt is not in the list either. run_child made it a
    # registered child, so __stop_children (script.rb:2052, :2288-2310) tears
    # it down on any kill, and during shutdown the process-wide drain owns
    # every script.
    before_dying do
      world.remove_overlay
      $UC_DIRECTOR = nil
    end
    $UC_DIRECTOR = self

    @unit = unit
    # "%d hunt(s)", not "budget %d". The old wording invited reading the
    # number as a leg, which `;uc-leg go N` in this same suite really does
    # mean. No leg count here on purpose: the itinerary does not exist yet
    # and building one for a banner would be a second build_itinerary call,
    # which the picker answers from live skills and so can answer differently.
    DRC.message(
      if unit == :cycles
        format('-- Hunting: %d full pass(es) through the itinerary. The director picks the legs. --',
               budget)
      else
        format('-- Hunting: %d hunt(s) to run. The director picks the legs. --', budget)
      end
    )
    DRC.message('  A stint that never reached the hunt loop does not spend the budget.', false)
    DRC.message('  ;p uc-director takes effect at the next cycle, not mid-stint.', false)

    session = UberCombat::Director::Session.new(world, duration_minutes: duration_minutes)
    session.run(budget, unit: @unit)
    record_run(world)
  end

  # The last run in this Lich process. D1 keeps no history: one run, replaced
  # by the next.
  def report
    run_record = $UC_DIRECTOR_LAST_RUN
    DRC.message('=== uc-director: last run ===')
    if run_record.nil?
      DRC.message('  No run has finished in this Lich session.', false)
      DRC.message('  Nothing is persisted in D1, so a restart clears this.', false)
      return
    end

    DRC.message(format('  stopped: %s%s', run_record[:reason],
                       run_record[:detail] ? format(' (%s)', run_record[:detail]) : ''), false)
    stints = Array(run_record[:stints])
    if stints.empty?
      DRC.message('  No stints ran.', false)
      return
    end

    stints.each do |stint|
      DRC.message(DirectorWorld.stint_line(stint), false)
      DirectorWorld.stint_deltas(stint).each { |line| DRC.message(line, false) }
    end
  end

  private

  # Deliberately builds NOTHING. An earlier draft printed the leg count here
  # and paid for it with a second build_itinerary call: the picker is stateless
  # and reads live skills (uc_zone_picker.rb:6-10), so two calls are two
  # answers, and a banner that disagrees with the itinerary printed under it is
  # worse than a banner with one less number on it.
  # The EFFECTIVE duration, not the constant. A character that set
  # hunt_duration_minutes must see its own number here, because this banner is
  # the only place a low test value left in a profile becomes visible again --
  # a five-minute hunt otherwise looks like a working thirty-minute one that
  # simply taught very little.
  def duration_minutes
    @duration_minutes ||=
      UberCombat::LegSettings.hunt_duration_minutes(get_settings) ||
      UberCombat::Director::DURATION_MINUTES
  end

  def banner
    duration = duration_minutes
    DRC.message(format('=== uc-director: %s, duration=%d min, timeout=%d s, health floor %d ===',
                       XMLData.name, duration,
                       UberCombat::Director.timeout_for(duration),
                       DirectorWorld::HEALTH_FLOOR))
  end

  # Everything plan mode needs, gathered without writing anything. The overlay
  # build is rescued because ArgumentError out of LegOverlay is a real (if
  # invariant-guard) possibility and a plan that crashed would tell a person
  # less than one that named the error.
  def plan_payload(world, itinerary, leg)
    duration = duration_minutes
    payload = { itinerary: itinerary, leg_index: 0, leg: leg, duration: duration,
                timeout: UberCombat::Director.timeout_for(duration),
                overlay: nil, decision: nil, path: world.overlay_path }
    return payload if leg.nil?

    begin
      overlay = world.overlay_for(leg, duration: duration)
      payload[:overlay] = overlay
      payload[:decision] = UberCombat::LegWriter.decide(overlay, world.existing_first_line)
    rescue ArgumentError => e
      DRC.message(format('uc-director: the overlay engine raised %s: %s', e.class, e.message))
    end
    payload
  end

  # The abort ladder runs before the first stint anyway, so without this a
  # character who is already hurt would "start" a run, hunt nothing, and then
  # be walked to the saferoom by the recovery path -- which looks like a
  # malfunction rather than a refusal. Same reasoning as uc-probe.lic:497-505.
  def preflight(world)
    reason = world.abort_reason
    if reason
      detail = world.abort_detail ? " (#{world.abort_detail})" : ''
      DRC.message(format('uc-director: NOT starting -- %s%s.', reason, detail))
      DRC.message('  A stint is half an hour of unattended combat. Heal up first.', false)
      return false
    end

    return false unless hunt_free?

    warn_about_foreign_overlay(world)
    true
  end

  # DEVIATION, and a deliberate one: the spec has this case reaching the core
  # as Script::StartError and stopping the run with :launch_refused (section
  # 6.4). That works, but it costs an itinerary build and one overlay WRITE
  # before it discovers a fact that was readable for free beforehand -- and
  # "hunting-buddy is already running" means something other than the director
  # is driving this character, so writing its profile overlay out from under
  # it is exactly the wrong move. The :launch_refused path stays intact for
  # every other cause and for a hunt that starts between here and the stint.
  def hunt_free?
    return true unless Script.running?('hunting-buddy')

    DRC.message('uc-director: NOT starting -- hunting-buddy is already running.')
    DRC.message('  Something else is driving this character. Stop it first, then re-run.', false)
    false
  end

  # A foreign file at the overlay path stops the WHOLE run at the first write
  # (spec 6.1), because every leg targets that one path. Saying so before the
  # run starts costs one file read.
  def warn_about_foreign_overlay(world)
    first_line = world.existing_first_line
    return if first_line.nil? || first_line == UberCombat::LegWriter::MARKER

    DRC.message('uc-director: WARNING -- a file this suite did not generate sits at the overlay path.')
    DRC.message("  #{world.overlay_path}", false)
    DRC.message('  Every leg writes there, so the first write will refuse and stop the run.', false)
  rescue StandardError => e
    DRC.message(format('uc-director: could not read the overlay path (%s). Continuing.', e.class))
  end

  def report_floor(world)
    DRC.message('-- Safety floor (checked before EVERY stint, never in a death handler) --')
    DRC.message(format('  health floor %d, current %s', DirectorWorld::HEALTH_FLOOR, DRStats.health), false)
    DRC.message(format('  spirit floor %d, current %s', DirectorWorld::SPIRIT_FLOOR, DRStats.spirit), false)
    reason = world.abort_reason
    DRC.message(format('  abort_reason right now: %s%s', reason || 'none',
                       world.abort_detail ? format(' (%s)', world.abort_detail) : ''), false)
    DRC.message('  Below the floor the director runs gosafe and stops. It never sends `exit`.', false)
  end

  # The world recorded the run as it rendered the :stopped announce, so this
  # needs no cooperation at all from whatever shape Session#run returns. That
  # is deliberate: the report survives a core that changes its return value.
  def record_run(world)
    return if world.last_stop.nil?

    $UC_DIRECTOR_LAST_RUN = world.last_stop
  end
end

# script is bound to Script.current by Lich's own script-launch eval
# (script.rb:176). vars[1], vars[2] are the whitespace-split tokens
# (script.rb:3098-3099). Same positional convention uc-leg.lic and
# uc-probe.lic use.
#
# No argument is the read-only plan -- the case that must never change.
mode = script.vars[1]

case mode
when nil
  UcDirector.new.plan
when /\Arun\z/i
  budget = script.vars[2]
  if budget.nil? || budget !~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/
    # Usage strings carry no angle brackets anywhere in this file. DRC.message
    # sends its text down a channel that strips anything shaped like a tag, so
    # a bracketed placeholder is silently deleted -- uc-probe's first live run
    # printed a command with its argument missing for exactly this reason.
    # N IS A COUNT OF HUNTS, NOT A LEG NUMBER. Worth being explicit about,
    # because `;uc-leg go 1` in this same suite DOES take a leg number, and
    # the two commands look identical. A real person read `run 4` as "run
    # leg 4" and asked whether a fourth leg existed.
    DRC.message('uc-director: run needs a number of hunts. Usage: ;uc-director run N')
    DRC.message('  N is HOW MANY hunts to run, not which leg to hunt. The director', false)
    DRC.message('  picks the leg itself and rotates through the itinerary as skills grow.', false)
    DRC.message('  ;uc-director run 4 means four hunts, not leg 4.', false)
    DRC.message('  There is no unbounded mode. One stint is half an hour of unattended combat.', false)
  else
    UcDirector.new.run(budget.to_i)
  end
when /\Acycles?\z/i
  # A CYCLE is one full pass through the itinerary, however many legs that is.
  # It is the stable unit: MAX_STINTS_PER_LEG = 1 makes one stint one leg
  # today, but the leg COUNT moves on its own as the skills-per-leg cap splits
  # a cluster or a rebuild returns a different itinerary -- so a stint budget
  # chosen to mean "one cycle" quietly stops meaning it.
  count = script.vars[2]
  if count.nil? || count !~ /\A[1-9][0-9]*\z/
    DRC.message('uc-director: cycles needs a number of passes. Usage: ;uc-director cycles N')
    DRC.message('  A cycle is one full pass through the itinerary, however many legs it holds.', false)
    DRC.message('  Use it when you mean "go round once" rather than "run this many hunts".', false)
    DRC.message('  There is no unbounded mode. One leg is half an hour of unattended combat.', false)
  else
    UcDirector.new.run(count.to_i, unit: :cycles)
  end
when /\Areport\z/i
  UcDirector.new.report
else
  DRC.message("uc-director: unknown argument '#{mode}'. " \
              'Usage: ;uc-director | ;uc-director run N | ;uc-director cycles N | ;uc-director report')
end
